---
import CodeListing from '@/components/ui/CodeListing.astro';
import Section from '@/components/ui/Section.astro';
import { OPTIMIZER } from '@/lib/viz/loss-surface';

const formats = [
  {
    name: 'Interactive figures',
    description:
      'Change a parameter and watch the model respond. Every core idea gets a figure you can manipulate.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Annotated code',
    description:
      'Short, complete Python that mirrors each figure — nothing hidden behind a library call.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Learning paths',
    description:
      'Ordered sequences that take you from prerequisite to practice without the guesswork.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Research notes',
    description:
      'Compact readings of papers and ideas, with the context needed to judge them.',
  },
];

// Rendered from the same constants that drive the hero figure, so the two cannot drift.
const listing = `import numpy as np

def descend(grad, theta, lr=${OPTIMIZER.learningRate}, beta=${OPTIMIZER.momentum}, steps=${OPTIMIZER.maxSteps}):
    """Gradient descent with momentum."""
    velocity = np.zeros_like(theta)
    path = [theta]
    for _ in range(steps):
        velocity = beta * velocity - lr * grad(theta)
        theta = theta + velocity
        path.append(theta)
    return np.array(path)`;
---

<Section
  id="method"
  index="02"
  label="Method"
  title="Show it, then name it, then use it."
>
  <div class="mb-12 max-w-2xl space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
    <p>
      A definition delivers the vocabulary without the object. The object is a surface, a boundary,
      a product of derivatives, a pattern of attention. Those can be drawn, and once drawn they can
      be changed. The change is the difference between recognizing a term and knowing what it
      refers to. A figure earns its place only when moving it moves a belief. Animation that merely
      plays is a video.
    </p>
    <p>
      Order is part of the teaching. A path is not a list of topics that share a tag. Each module
      says what should be understood, which ideas that understanding depends on, why those ideas
      are the ones that matter, and what the next module needs from this one. Without the handoff,
      the later page is a new subject instead of a consequence.
    </p>
    <p>
      The same restraint applies to the research log. A posted entry points at a source. A planned
      entry states a question and does not pretend to have answered it. The four formats below are
      the instruments. None of them is a long article standing in for the picture.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-x-10 gap-y-12 xl:grid-cols-12">
    <dl class="border-t border-line xl:col-span-5">
      {
        formats.map((format) => (
          <div class="border-b border-line py-5">
            <dt class="font-medium text-ink">{format.name}</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1.5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
              {format.description}
            </dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <div class="min-w-0 xl:col-span-7">
      <CodeListing code={listing} lang="python" title="descend.py" number="01" />
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        The figure at the top of this page, as code: the same update rule and the same
        hyper-parameters.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
